# Add this setting to the EXISTING trusted environment file used by the resident host.
# Do not copy the token to a workspace, JSON config, renderer, Git, or launchd plist.
# For the monorepo daily launcher this is the repository root .env (../../.env).
# If RUNLOOM_HOST_ENV_FILE is set, that file is the source instead.
# Obtain a bot token privately from Telegram's official @BotFather.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
# Optional: only Telegram uses this proxy, not the model or other modules.
# Use your existing HTTP/HTTPS proxy; no direct fallback or send retry.
TELEGRAM_PROXY_URL=
# Apply while idle: stop the resident host, then explicitly enable it again.
# Connect and confirm your account in Serika -> module capabilities -> Telegram.
